INT. ABANDONED RADIO OBSERVATORY - CONTROL ROOM - DAWN

Dead consoles. A dish groans overhead. Grey light leaks through a shattered window.

COLETTE ABIODUN-FENWICK, 40s, bleeding from the scalp, sits slumped against a rack of machines. Her pistol lies beside her hand, slide locked back.

Across the room, CASSIUS "CASS" DRAGOMIR, 30s, in a torn parka, stands against the far wall with his hands up, a sat phone dangling from one finger.

Between them lies a third figure, face down, motionless: NESTOR PELLEGRINI-OYELOWO, 50s, in a lab coat, one hand still clutching a flash drive.

COLETTE
You brought him here.

CASS
I brought a doctor.

COLETTE
You brought a corpse.

CASS
He was breathing when we arrived.

COLETTE
Not when I did.

Cass lowers a hand. Colette lifts the empty pistol, hand shaking, and levels it.

CASS
It's empty.

COLETTE
You don't know that.

CASS
I counted.

COLETTE
You counted wrong.

CASS
Colette--

COLETTE
(whisper)
Don't use my name.

A cough. Nestor stirs. Colette and Cass both leap, he toward the body, she toward the pistol, and they collide in the middle of the floor, knocking over a chair. The sat phone skids across the tile.

Nestor rolls onto his back, wheezing. Opens one eye.

NESTOR
Don't shoot.

COLETTE
Nestor. You're alive.

NESTOR
Barely. Cass?

CASS
Here.

NESTOR
Did you call it in?

CASS
The signal's dead.

NESTOR
The dish.

CASS
The dish is broken.

Nestor drags himself to a sitting position. He holds up the flash drive, fingers trembling.

NESTOR
Then we do it the old way. Upload by hand.

COLETTE
To what?

NESTOR
There's a transmitter in the basement.

COLETTE
Then we go down.

CASS
It could be mined.

NESTOR
It could.

COLETTE
(standing, dusting her coat)
Or it could be our only way home.

Cass stares at her. At Nestor. At the drive.

CASS
Fine. But I carry it.

NESTOR
You'll drop it.

CASS
I will not.

Colette snatches the drive from Nestor and tosses it to Cass without a word. He catches it one-handed.

CASS (CONT'D)
(deadpan)
Thank you.

COLETTE
Don't get used to it.

They help Nestor to his feet, one on each arm. Together they shuffle toward the stairwell door, three silhouettes against the grey window.

Behind them, the dish gives a long metallic groan and turns, by a degree, toward the sky.

INT. OBSERVATORY STAIRWELL - CONTINUOUS

Concrete spiral. Dust. A single bulb swinging.

Colette leads, Cass behind, Nestor between. Their footsteps ring.

NESTOR
I never thanked you.

CASS
For what?

NESTOR
For the doctor line. In the car.

CASS
I didn't lie.

NESTOR
You said I was a doctor.

CASS
You are.

NESTOR
Of physics.

CASS
That counts.

COLETTE
Quiet. Down here.

They reach the basement door. Padlock. She raises the pistol, finds the slide locked back, curses, and swings it like a hammer. The lock breaks.

The door opens on a black room. Somewhere a relay clicks.

COLETTE (CONT'D)
Lights?

NESTOR
Third switch.

Cass finds it. Fluorescent tubes flicker alive. A rack of ancient radio gear, a desk, a chair. And on the desk, a single working microphone.

NESTOR (CONT'D)
(whispering)
There she is.

Cass plugs in the drive. Nestor sits and leans toward the microphone. Colette and Cass stand on either side of him, silent, hands on his shoulders.

NESTOR (CONT'D)
(into the microphone)
This is Nestor Pellegrini-Oyelowo, calling anyone. Anyone at all.

Static. A long beat of hiss. Then, faint, from far away, a voice rises from the speaker.

Colette closes her eyes. Cass lets out a breath he has been holding since the car.
